      "verified": true,
      "fine_trace_step": 5,
      "description": "Reads the attacker-controlled `nx_action_encap` property slice into typed parser state by setting `ofp_prop = nae->props` and deriving `props_len` from `nae->len`. On the saved witness action this materializes one 8-byte property for the loop to decode."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "r_encap_must_track_saved_offset_before_n_props_write",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "file": "lib/ofp-actions.c",
      "function": "decode_NXAST_RAW_ENCAP",
      "line": 4346,
      "operands": [
        "(size_t) ((char *) encap - (char *) out->base)",
        "out->size"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "(size_t) ((char *) encap - (char *) out->base)",
        "right": "out->size"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_encap_must_track_saved_offset_before_n_props_write",
      "fine_trace_step": 6,
      "description": "The function calls `decode_ed_prop(&ofp_prop, out, &props_len)` while keeping `encap` as a raw pointer into `out`, but it never refreshes that pointer after the property loop may grow `out`. The fix saves `encap`'s offset before the loop and reloads it with `ofpbuf_at_assert()` before the later writes."
    },
    {
